{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Reachability analysis (resolves the original 'dead code?' question):\n\n- PLAN-REVIEW mid-run arm: REACHABLE in production. interpreter._run_batch calls runner.run(req, rc.runner) with NO try, so batch-runner raises propagate RAW out of run_workflow. ProductionBatchRunner -> run_pass1: the Pass-1 chunk pool explicitly re-raises LLMUnavailableError ('except LLMUnavailableError: raise', pass1.py), and container_stage._run_container's warm-call abort raises BOTH LLMUnavailableError and LLMInputRejectedError up through run_pass1. The original probe failed because it raised in the AGENT-step path, which interpreter._run_leaf absorbs into a failed StepResult ('except Exception' at the dispatch site) — the batch path is the raw seam.\n\n- CODE-REVIEW mid-run arm: DEFENSIVE seam contract today, not proven-reachable. CodeReviewBatchRunner._run_criterion translates a runner's LLMUnavailableError into the kernel's SystemicDiscoveryError, which discovery.execute_stage ABSORBS (systemic_abort=True, unit marked failed — no re-raise); other LLMErrors become LocalOperationExhausted (also absorbed); agent-step raises are absorbed by _run_leaf. No in-tree production path raising these types out of the code-review run_workflow was found. Disposition per the coverage-only mandate: the arm is PINNED at the run_workflow seam (test-as-contract) rather than removed — removal is a separate design decision; this comment records the evidence.\n\n- CONTAINER warm abort: reachable and now driven directly (real _run_container, passes.pass1_container monkeypatched at the model-call boundary)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787383724792778001,"uuid":"9bbe8473-2299-403b-b47e-262fac0b3068"}